    capability_group_from_unsound_under_value_semantics_2026-08-09, 0, "Doc: design correction required; only P2's library ships the corrected shape, the .from() API itself is unchanged [PATH DRIFT: src/lib/nog"
    capability_group_from_unsound_under_value_semantics_2026-08-09, 1, "Triage 2026-11-04 on seed 0b2c3d015b7: debug_target_ref_spec 71/71 pass in 12.6s (library-side corrected single-value group shape holds). Remaining item is P0 desugar of .from() (lint detector dynamic_capability_acquire.spl only flags spellings). NOTE premise risk: the unsoundness rests on classes having value semantics; other lanes report an interpreter class-ref default flip (SIMPLE_INTERP_CLASS_REF=1) is pending - if it lands the premise changes and this row must be re-scoped. QUESTION: is class-ref flip the intended direction (then close as obsolete) or do value-class semantics stay?"
    capability_group_from_unsound_under_value_semantics_2026-08-09, 2, "2026-11-09 lane-p2-3: closed-obsolete. Owner decision 2026-11-06 classes are reference types; release src value.rs class_ref default on (SIMPLE_INTERP_CLASS_REF unset -> true). Probe var b=a; a.bump(): JIT a=1 b=1, interpreter with flag a=1 b=1 (shared bin/simple.exe predates 6c7b4db3d39). Remaining .from() desugar is feature work, tracked by TODO in dynamic_capability_acquire.spl."

